WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.510
Three words: «vingt», «vent», «vont».

2
00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:06.400
Twenty, wind, they go.

3
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:08.050
They may sound close to you.

4
00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:11.360
To a French ear, they're
three different words.

5
00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:14.510
Now the opposite puzzle: «pain»,

6
00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:17.790
«fin», «faim». Bread, end, hunger.

7
00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:20.270
Different spellings. One sound.

8
00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:22.010
How can they match so exactly,

9
00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:24.060
when they look so different?

10
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.300
In this mission, you'll
follow the air as it

11
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.070
leaves a speaker's head.

12
00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:32.180
Then you'll sort words by ear
into four buckets in the lab.

13
00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:35.360
Your mission: find out how
three different spellings can

14
00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:37.150
end up as one sound.
